          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"feynman-parameter-polynomials\">Feynman-parameter polynomials</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For the two-loop denominators <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||((k+l)^2-m^2||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||((k-l)\\cdot p+\\delta||)</marimo-tex>,\nwith <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p^2=s||)</marimo-tex>, the quadratic loop matrix is singular. Feynkit still returns\nits algebraic polynomials <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(U=0||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(F=sxy^2||)</marimo-tex>.\nThese polynomials alone do not define an integration formula or establish\nthat the integral vanishes.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
